  "id": "chaos1",
  "name": "1st Chaos Lord · Chiral Valley",
  "bundle": false,
  "once": true,
  "notes": "The whole 1st Chaos Lord line in one run: the five Chiral chains in /mobius, /faerie, /cornelis, /relativity and /hydra, then Escherion himself, then the Phoenix Hunter the saga pays out. It is a one-pass route (`once`), so a quest this character has handed in is remembered and never taken again, and the run stops itself once nothing is left; each pass works on whatever is already in hand, otherwise the next quest of the chain the server actually offers, so a restart picks up where the character is. Nine of the 26 are not fights: 246, 251, 260, 261, 262, 263, 266, 267 and 271 are map items, clicked by the id the map's own sparkle sends, on a loop until the quest asks for nothing. Those stop combat and stand on the Blank cell first, where nothing can reach them, because a click is a packet and does not need the sparkle in sight; 271 wants three items, so it cycles through 52, 51 and 50 instead of waiting on one. A fight step hands over the moment the quest reads complete rather than finishing the mob, and every turn-in stops combat first, so a finished quest never keeps the boss angry. Loot is claimed as it falls (`pickup`): these quests pay real drops with names a route cannot list ahead of time. The last steps buy the free Phoenix Hunter from shop 946 in /freakitiki, the saga's own reward; if the shop is not unlocked the route ends quietly instead of stalling on it. 253 and 254 are side quests the line does not need.",
